        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="1010" n="914" xml:id="pg914"/>

                <head>No. 580.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gadwalader to Mr.
                    Cushing.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 7,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 76.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your dispatch No. 98, of
                    the 16th ultimo, relative to the alleged transfer of Puerto Rico to Germany, I
                    have to state that your action in regard to the matter, as therein set forth, is
                    approved.</p>
                <p>The Department has never placed any faith in the rumors regarding the alleged
                    transfer.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN L. CAD WALADER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                            Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
